s gives the country to  magneto as a mutant homeland  under his leadership it grows into  something much larger than we see in the  Dark Phoenix one of the Dark Phoenix is  more mysterious minor characters is a  rekey one of the Genosha pnes magneto  brings with him when he attempts to kill  Jean Grey his powers revolve around his  long hair which he uses to  grapple or strike opponents while he's  initially an enemy of the x-men he's  arrested with the heroes and fights  alongside them in their battle against  the d'bari on the train Parikh II  doesn't appear in the comics it was  initially reported Andrew Stellan would  be playing a different character IGN  reported that Stalin's character was Red  Lotus in Australian Chinese character  from Xtreme x-men whose powers have  nothing to do with hair manipulation not  that any of that matters all that much  Ricci essentially disappears from the  movie during the train battle when  Professor X makes a speech after  receiving an award from the president  one of the white house guests is Chris  Claremont a writer whose work on the  x-men comics helped make them the  household names they are now he started  writing x-men in 1975 and wrote them  continuously until 1991 he returns to  the franchise occasionally even now he  wrote the first Wolverine miniseries  with artist Frank Miller and when Logan  finally got his own ongoing series  Claremont was its first scribe Claremont  established a foundation for much of  what we see in the films it was  Claremont who introduced the idea that  magneto is a Holocaust survivor and that  his actions stem from his horrific  experiences during that time and of  course it was Claremont and collaborator  John Byrne who crafted the Dark Phoenix  saga we had no expectations at all when  we did the story we just want to do a  really great story there's a lot of  mystery surrounding Jessica Chastain's  character leading up to the release of  Dark Phoenix we now know she plays Buch  a member 